WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:08.570
“It is time to officially recognize Jerusalem
as the capital of Israel.”

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:14.280
The US has officially moved its embassy in
Israel from Tel Aviv to Jerusalem, and in

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.660
doing so, President Trump

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.940
has reversed decades of consensus about
the city’s status.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.560
While Israeli leaders celebrated,

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.500
Palestinians denounced the move,

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.860
deepening divides between two sides of a conflict
that is 70 years old.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.500
“We’re hearing live fire…”

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:31.780
“Rising death toll…”

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.070
“Quite a juxtaposition…”

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:37.000
Here are 5 things to know about Jerusalem
and why it’s so contentious.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:47.180
Israel has controlled West Jerusalem since
1949.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:52.960
During the Six Day War, Israel captured East
Jerusalem and annexed that half of the city.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:58.720
But the international community considers
East Jerusalem occupied territory, whose fate

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:03.340
needs to be part of a negotiated deal between
Israel and the Palestinians.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:09.660
In 1980, after Israel passed a law declaring
a united Jerusalem the capital,

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.480
the United Nations
condemned the annexation.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:17.400
Palestinians want to divide the city and make
East Jerusalem the capital of a future

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.400
Palestinian state,

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:22.480
while Israelis want a unified Jerusalem to
be their capital.

00:01:27.749 --> 00:01:30.840
During peace process negotiations for the
Oslo Accords,

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.909
the issue of Jerusalem was initially

00:01:32.909 --> 00:01:35.380
set aside to avoid derailing the talks.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.220
Any successful peace initiative in the future
would likely need to resolve the conflicting

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:44.360
claims to the land.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.840
Control of Jerusalem has been a trigger for
violence many times in the past.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.509
The contested area of East Jerusalem is home
to some of the holiest sites in the world

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:00.320
for Jews and Muslims.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.709
It is the site where Judaism’s two sacred
temples once stood.

00:02:04.709 --> 00:02:07.270
And the site where the prophet Mohammed ascended
to heaven.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:12.080
The trouble is that the sites for Muslims
and Jews exist on the same land.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:14.580
There’s a precarious power share in place.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:18.700
Israeli officials control who has access to
the complex.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.220
But Muslims have religious control inside.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.950
Jews can enter but aren’t allowed to pray.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.080
Instead, they use the Western Wall.

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:28.840
The second intifada began in 2000,

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.220
when then-opposition
leader Ariel Sharon visited the Temple Mount

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.160
to assert Israel’s right to the complex.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.920
Palestinians protested and were met with tear
gas and rubber bullets.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:46.100
The violence lasted five years and killed
more than 3,000 Palestinians

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.320
and nearly 1,000 Israelis,

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.900
with thousands more wounded.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:59.120
In the early 70's, 16 countries had embassies
in Jerusalem, including the Netherlands and

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.120
Colombia.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:05.739
But after the UN Security Council condemned
the annexation of East Jerusalem in 1980.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:06.760
member states left.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.360
Then, Trump signaled a change in policy,

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.820
and Guatemala and Paraguay also announced they

00:03:11.829 --> 00:03:13.810
are moving their embassies to Jerusalem

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:17.080
And it's possible that more countries will
follow America’s lead.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.680
Though Congress passed a law to relocate

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.420
the U.S. embassy to Jerusalem more than 20 years ago,

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:32.060
the law includes a loophole that allows the
president to delay the relocation for the

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.580
sake of national security.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.360
Every sitting president --

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.080
Clinton, Bush,
Obama --

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.000
has used this power and signed the

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.360
waiver every 6 months.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:44.180
President Trump signed the waiver in June
2017,

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:47.160
and again in December 2017,

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:47.660
but also

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:52.849
signaled he would begin the process of moving
the embassy from Tel Aviv to Jerusalem.

00:03:52.849 --> 00:03:56.670
And in May of 2018, he carried out his pledge.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:59.700
The embassy move came at an already a tense
time.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:05.040
Tens of thousands of Palestinians have spent
the past few weeks holding protests on the

00:04:05.049 --> 00:04:06.960
border between Gaza and Israel,

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.060
that weren’t
tied to the embassy move.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:13.790
Dozens of Palestinians had been killed even
before the embassy opened.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:17.900
While President Trump was careful not to call
Jerusalem an “undivided” capital.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:23.720
Israeli prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu
said just that at the US embassy opening.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:29.140
“God Bless Jerusalem, the eternal undivided
capital of Israel.”

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:35.060
But opposition to Trump’s declarations and
the embassy move has been growing.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:40.090
And as lines are drawn and the fight for Jerusalem
intensifies, the future of Israeli-Palestinian

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:42.199
stability is once again at risk.

